Subject: [PATCH 10556/11362] Land generator-provenance helpers, tested and
 deliberately inert (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6790)

The measurement half of the 2026-08-31 finding: a 22-hour adapter-free run over 9
games produced numbers that could not be read as an e3 result, because nothing
recorded whether each game HAD a generator. Of 23 server logs from that run,
exactly ONE had completions; the other 22 were failed starts. A row reading
`levels=2, efficiency=0.1025` was indistinguishable between the e3 cascade solving
it and the explorer floor solving it with no model at all.

`generator_provenance()` reports the reachable backend (URL, model path, the
server's OBSERVED model, reuse check, n_ctx, ffn_cpu_layers).
`completion_counters()` snapshots the proposer's monotone channel counters
(REQ-ARC-WMTE-6710), so differencing two reads gives the completions ONE game
consumed -- zero means no model was reached, whatever the levels say.

Two deliberate choices. Provenance never raises: an unreadable attribute is
RECORDED as unreadable, because provenance that breaks the run it describes is
worse than none. And the snapshot is a COPY -- a shared reference would difference
to zero and report "no model reached" for every game, inverting the signal.

SHIPPED INERT, ON PURPOSE, AND SAID SO. Nothing calls this yet. Editing
arc_leaderboard_eval.py makes 5 artifacts stale that cite it as provenance, and
artifact-freshness-lint refuses until each is rebuilt and diffed -- the same guard
whose fail-open was fixed on 08-29, so working around it was not an option. One
rebuild is already done and moved ZERO measured values (7 fields, all bookkeeping;
answer line identical), which is good evidence the wiring is additive but is not
evidence about the other four.

This is the "implemented beside the call site" shape this session caught three
times. It is acceptable here only because it is announced rather than assumed: a
test named
`test_the_call_site_assertion_is_deliberately_absent_until_the_wiring_lands` FAILS
the moment the wiring lands and carries the exact assertions to restore, the
prepared 44-line diff is preserved as eval_wiring.patch, and the remaining
